1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,417
This is Lexi. Lexi, Kara.

2
00:00:01,418 --> 00:00:02,419
Where’s Allie?

3
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:04,169
- We broke up, Lex. - [LEXI] What?

4
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:05,796
But, you know, we all saw this coming.

5
00:00:05,797 --> 00:00:07,214
[LEXI] I’m sorry to say this, okay?

6
00:00:07,215 --> 00:00:09,718
But it seems like you and Kara have more chemistry!

7
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:11,845
[LEXI] Okay, anyway!

8
00:00:11,886 --> 00:00:14,180
- Are you okay, bro? - I got friendzoned, bro.

9
00:00:14,222 --> 00:00:15,098
Don’t be sad.

10
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:16,432
[QUINITO] I’m happy for Jao.

11
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:17,767
You and Kara look good together.

12
00:00:18,184 --> 00:00:19,394
I think...

13
00:00:19,728 --> 00:00:21,020
Kara also likes you.

14
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:22,647
What's the status between the two of you?

15
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:25,399
We just like spending a lot of time together.

16
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:27,193
- [ARCHIE] Hi, Kara. - [KARA] Archie!

17
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:29,237
- I’ve missed you so much. - I’ve missed you!

18
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:30,697
Jao, this is Archie.

19
00:00:30,739 --> 00:00:31,531
I’m Jao.

20
00:00:31,573 --> 00:00:33,241
So, you’re here for vacation?

21
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:34,366
No, I’m here for Kara.

22
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:35,285
Um...

23
00:00:35,286 --> 00:00:37,787
Archie, can I bring Jao along next week?

24
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:39,205
Yeah, man. Is that okay?

25
00:00:39,456 --> 00:00:41,957
What made you decide to volunteer today, Quinito?

26
00:00:41,958 --> 00:00:45,795
I also want to give back to the kids before I go back to Manila.

27
00:00:45,962 --> 00:00:47,172
You’re leaving?

28
00:00:48,423 --> 00:00:50,425
Bro, we’re really gonna miss you.

29
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:52,552
Kara told me you work for Young Horizon?

30
00:00:52,594 --> 00:00:55,472
You won’t stop until you find out what I do for a living, huh?

31
00:00:55,513 --> 00:00:57,015
I'm just curious, bro.

32
00:00:57,056 --> 00:00:58,266
Do we have a problem?

33
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:02,187
So we’ve prepared some compost materials,

34
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:04,272
so you guys can try it yourselves.

35
00:01:04,647 --> 00:01:06,149
Why don’t you just watch us...

36
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:07,233
Kara?

37
00:01:07,692 --> 00:01:10,111
I’ll partner up with Jao.

38
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:17,619
[LEXI] We can be partners, bro.

39
00:01:17,869 --> 00:01:18,870
Teach me.

40
00:01:19,287 --> 00:01:20,287
It will be fun.

41
00:01:20,288 --> 00:01:20,997
Bro.

42
00:01:21,456 --> 00:01:22,248
Sure.

43
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:25,960
I don’t know anything about this.

44
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,837
It’s okay. Just follow my lead.

45
00:01:28,838 --> 00:01:29,631
Okay.

46
00:01:33,134 --> 00:01:36,221
So, let's start with dried leaves.

47
00:01:37,138 --> 00:01:40,433
[KARA] Dried leaves are rich in carbon.

48
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:45,021
They’ll help balance the compost as it breaks down.

49
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:48,191
Just add more...

50
00:01:50,193 --> 00:01:51,986
And this is... bok choy?

51
00:01:52,195 --> 00:01:53,195
Yeah.

52
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:54,948
So just get...

53
00:02:10,046 --> 00:02:12,173
Okay. Next one.

54
00:02:39,742 --> 00:02:41,244
You can add some more.

55
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:47,959
Why?

56
00:02:49,335 --> 00:02:51,421
It's just amazing how...

57
00:02:52,672 --> 00:02:53,965
as I get to know you,

58
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:57,427
the more I discover how knowledgeable you are.

59
00:02:58,261 --> 00:03:00,263
And I find your intelligence...

60
00:03:01,264 --> 00:03:02,599
very attractive.

61
00:03:05,476 --> 00:03:06,811
[KARA CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

62
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:08,271
Oh, please.

63
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:09,606
[JAO AND KARA CHUCKLES]

64
00:03:11,941 --> 00:03:13,943
Bro, I know you don’t know me,

65
00:03:13,985 --> 00:03:15,361
but I’m just saying…

66
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:17,739
That’s a lost cause.

67
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,241
What?

68
00:03:21,618 --> 00:03:22,827
Kara and Jao!

69
00:03:22,994 --> 00:03:23,953
It’s done!

70
00:03:23,995 --> 00:03:25,663
You don't stand a chance.

71
00:03:25,705 --> 00:03:27,415
[IMITATES EXPLOSION] None!

72
00:03:27,832 --> 00:03:29,167
Just look at them.

73
00:03:30,627 --> 00:03:32,211
[LEXI] Do you know what that’s called?

74
00:03:32,629 --> 00:03:36,215
Which, incidentally, is happening right here, right now.

75
00:03:37,175 --> 00:03:37,967
[LEXI CLAPS]

76
00:03:38,092 --> 00:03:40,094
They've got chemistry, bro.

77
00:03:40,136 --> 00:03:41,846
That’s chemistry.

78
00:03:43,556 --> 00:03:46,351
And all you have in your hands is soil

79
00:03:46,601 --> 00:03:48,394
and a bunch of crap.

80
00:04:03,868 --> 00:04:08,373
[ALON BY JL]

81
00:05:22,071 --> 00:05:32,582
[CHILDREN TALKING]

82
00:05:32,623 --> 00:05:34,041
Hello, everyone!

83
00:05:34,042 --> 00:05:36,085
- Hi! - Hi!

84
00:05:36,127 --> 00:05:39,172
I’m Quinito, and today,

85
00:05:39,213 --> 00:05:42,133
we’ll be reading a story by Ica!

86
00:05:42,175 --> 00:05:43,175
Give her a round of applause!

87
00:05:43,176 --> 00:05:46,679
[CLAPPING]

88
00:05:46,929 --> 00:05:49,223
Today’s story is about...

89
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:50,641
Inoy.

90
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:53,186
“Inoy and the Waves.”

91
00:05:53,895 --> 00:05:56,605
It's about the waves of Siargao

92
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:59,609
and how Inoy was swept away by them.

93
00:06:01,611 --> 00:06:03,612
Okay, let’s start. Are you guys ready?

94
00:06:03,613 --> 00:06:05,615
- [KIDS] Yes! - Okay.

95
00:06:06,032 --> 00:06:10,119
Inoy couldn’t remember how the waves carried him

96
00:06:10,161 --> 00:06:12,163
to the island of Siargao.

97
00:06:13,831 --> 00:06:15,332
[QUINITO] All he knew

98
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:17,835
was that he felt lonely where he was.

99
00:06:17,877 --> 00:06:19,879
And when the waves sang to him,

100
00:06:20,129 --> 00:06:22,840
he followed them right away.

101
00:06:23,966 --> 00:06:25,760
On the island of Siargao,

102
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:28,304
he met many friends.

103
00:06:28,721 --> 00:06:30,515
Mangroves,

104
00:06:30,848 --> 00:06:31,849
fish,

105
00:06:32,350 --> 00:06:33,351
turtles...

106
00:06:33,518 --> 00:06:35,103
But one stood out the most...

107
00:06:35,144 --> 00:06:40,441
A pearl that shone as brightly as the sun.

108
00:06:42,401 --> 00:06:44,402
[QUINITO] He’d been warned many times

109
00:06:44,403 --> 00:06:48,116
not to go near the mysterious pearl

110
00:06:48,366 --> 00:06:51,577
as its brilliant glow could burn him.

111
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:55,331
But Inoy was always stubborn.

112
00:06:55,373 --> 00:06:58,167
He wanted to get to know the pearl, even if it meant getting hurt.

113
00:07:00,545 --> 00:07:02,171
Do you like libraries?

114
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:04,090
Oh! Yes, Sir Han.

115
00:07:04,298 --> 00:07:07,425
You can’t tell, but I'm always browsing.

116
00:07:07,426 --> 00:07:09,427
Because in the library,

117
00:07:09,428 --> 00:07:12,723
this is where I can see all parts of the world.

118
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:16,102
Then you should see the New York Public Library.

119
00:07:16,394 --> 00:07:17,812
It’s really big!

120
00:07:18,354 --> 00:07:21,064
And I think you would also enjoy the

121
00:07:21,065 --> 00:07:22,692
Bodleian in Oxford.

122
00:07:22,859 --> 00:07:25,862
It’s so peaceful and quiet there.

123
00:07:26,445 --> 00:07:28,364
- Oh! - And...

124
00:07:28,698 --> 00:07:30,700
one more library in Amsterdam,

125
00:07:30,741 --> 00:07:33,411
near the harbor, which has a cafe on the rooftop…

126
00:07:33,786 --> 00:07:35,663
You know, it’s really amazing.

127
00:07:36,247 --> 00:07:36,956
Wow!

128
00:07:36,957 --> 00:07:38,374
You know what, Sir Han?

129
00:07:39,041 --> 00:07:40,710
Just hearing you describe it,

130
00:07:40,751 --> 00:07:43,754
I can already picture it and I already want to go!

131
00:07:43,796 --> 00:07:44,796
[HAN BIN AND PEARL LAUGH]

132
00:07:44,797 --> 00:07:47,425
[PEARL] Wow, you've been to a lot of places, Sir Han.

133
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:51,219
Wait, in Korea, is there a library also?

134
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:54,849
Yeah! We also have amazing libraries in Korea, too.

135
00:07:55,391 --> 00:07:57,185
You should see the...

136
00:07:57,226 --> 00:07:59,228
Starfield Library in Seoul.

137
00:07:59,562 --> 00:08:03,774
You’ve been to all the libraries you mentioned?

138
00:08:05,526 --> 00:08:06,235
No…

139
00:08:06,236 --> 00:08:09,655
I just heard all about those libraries...

140
00:08:10,031 --> 00:08:11,741
from my…

141
00:08:11,949 --> 00:08:12,950
…from my friend!

142
00:08:13,034 --> 00:08:14,118
- Yes, from a friend. - A friend.

143
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,577
- Yes. - Okay.

144
00:08:15,578 --> 00:08:20,208
- You want to go to the bathroom? - [QUINITO] ...And Inoy asked his friends, the waves,

145
00:08:20,416 --> 00:08:23,502
to carry the pearl wherever...

146
00:08:24,212 --> 00:08:25,213
it wished to go.

147
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:29,966
[QUINITO] Though his hands blistered from holding it,

148
00:08:29,967 --> 00:08:31,677
he had no regrets.

149
00:08:32,803 --> 00:08:34,222
To Inoy,

150
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:37,892
those blisters were a reminder of his friend, the pearl.

151
00:08:41,729 --> 00:08:44,023
Goodbye, my friend, pearl.

152
00:08:44,649 --> 00:08:46,651
I hope you won’t forget me.

153
00:08:51,113 --> 00:08:56,535
[CLAPPING]

154
00:08:56,577 --> 00:08:58,079
[QUINITO] Did you enjoy it?

155
00:08:58,621 --> 00:09:00,623
[BACKGROUND CHATTER]

156
00:09:00,665 --> 00:09:02,874
What should I upload?

157
00:09:02,875 --> 00:09:04,502
Hm... What do you think?

158
00:09:04,710 --> 00:09:06,211
This one? This?

159
00:09:06,212 --> 00:09:07,337
- Nice. [PEARL LAUGHS] - Or this?

160
00:09:07,338 --> 00:09:08,756
Ariel, why is...

161
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:12,551
Sir Han facing away in all your photos?

162
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:16,806
I told you, he hates photos and videos.

163
00:09:18,266 --> 00:09:19,267
Why, though?

164
00:09:20,059 --> 00:09:22,353
No idea. Maybe he doesn’t want to be famous.

165
00:09:23,938 --> 00:09:25,856
Or maybe he doesn’t want to get hate.

166
00:09:26,148 --> 00:09:27,441
Is he a celebrity or something?

167
00:09:28,651 --> 00:09:29,734
[QUINITO] Good idea!

168
00:09:29,735 --> 00:09:32,238
What if he really is a celebrity in Korea?

169
00:09:32,822 --> 00:09:34,073
You know, someone messaged me,

170
00:09:34,115 --> 00:09:35,950
looking for a Song Ji Hoon.

171
00:09:37,868 --> 00:09:38,869
Who’s that?

172
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,162
I don’t know!

173
00:09:49,046 --> 00:09:50,840
[KARA] We’ll water them later.

174
00:09:51,215 --> 00:09:52,133
[LEXI] Just say the word.

175
00:09:52,174 --> 00:09:53,801
I’ll take care of Archie.

176
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:56,262
You know I’ve been taking jiu-jitsu lessons?

177
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:58,681
Forget it. Just ignore him.

178
00:09:59,181 --> 00:09:59,974
[LEXI SIGHS]

179
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:03,519
He’s just jealous because Kara’s obviously into you, too.

180
00:10:05,688 --> 00:10:07,690
Hey, wipe that grin off your face.

181
00:10:07,732 --> 00:10:09,025
Make a move!

182
00:10:09,775 --> 00:10:10,776
Lex…

183
00:10:11,527 --> 00:10:13,237
actually, it’s not on me.

184
00:10:13,529 --> 00:10:14,822
I like Kara a lot.

185
00:10:15,865 --> 00:10:16,866
But...

186
00:10:17,158 --> 00:10:18,868
I have to respect her timeline.

187
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:20,411
Wow.

188
00:10:20,745 --> 00:10:22,913
Slow and long courtship.

189
00:10:22,955 --> 00:10:23,956
So old school!

190
00:10:24,248 --> 00:10:25,750
But I love it! [LEXI GIGGLES]

191
00:10:27,209 --> 00:10:29,211
[JAO] All that's missing is Harana (traditional Filipino serenade), right?

192
00:10:30,671 --> 00:10:31,881
What's Harana?

193
00:10:33,090 --> 00:10:34,383
What do you mean?

194
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:36,135
[JAO STUTTERS]

195
00:10:36,177 --> 00:10:38,888
You’re making me feel too old.

196
00:10:39,138 --> 00:10:40,139
Harana?

197
00:10:40,514 --> 00:10:41,515
[LEXI SCOFFS]

198
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:43,642
[ARCHIE] Kara, I’ll just check on the guests.

199
00:10:43,684 --> 00:10:44,268
- [KARA] Okay. - [LEXI] Kara!

200
00:10:44,310 --> 00:10:46,604
- [LEXI] Thank you for inviting me here! - [KARA] You’re welcome!

201
00:10:46,645 --> 00:10:49,440
[LEXI] You’re right. I learned a lot here.

202
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:52,401
I had fun, except…

203
00:10:52,443 --> 00:10:53,444
[KARA LAUGHS]

204
00:10:53,486 --> 00:10:54,653
Sorry about Archie.

205
00:10:54,695 --> 00:10:56,572
He’s a little blunt.

206
00:10:56,614 --> 00:10:58,699
But once you get to know him, he’s actually a nice guy.

207
00:10:58,741 --> 00:11:01,327
- Nice? Him? I doubt it. - [KARA CHUCKLES]

208
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:04,663
Well, since I'm leaving anyway, whatever.

209
00:11:05,873 --> 00:11:07,249
You’re not extending your stay?

210
00:11:07,291 --> 00:11:09,377
No, don’t tempt me!

211
00:11:09,418 --> 00:11:12,213
If I end up quitting my job, I won’t know what to do next.

212
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:13,673
Maybe I should quit?

213
00:11:13,714 --> 00:11:14,714
- Anyway… - [KARA LAUGHS]

214
00:11:14,715 --> 00:11:17,050
[LEXI] I have two more nights left in Siargao.

215
00:11:17,051 --> 00:11:18,552
I’m going to make the most of them.

216
00:11:19,845 --> 00:11:20,846
Bye, Kara!

217
00:11:21,305 --> 00:11:22,723
[LEXI] It might be short and sweet,

218
00:11:22,765 --> 00:11:23,849
[LEXI] but I had fun.

219
00:11:23,891 --> 00:11:25,100
Yay! I’m so glad.

220
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:26,811
- [KARA AND LEXI LAUGH] - And this guy?

221
00:11:27,269 --> 00:11:28,646
He’s one of the good ones.

222
00:11:28,687 --> 00:11:30,481
[LEXI] Trust me. I can vouch for him.

223
00:11:30,523 --> 00:11:31,523
All right, enough.

224
00:11:31,524 --> 00:11:33,734
Isn’t that guy from the dating app waiting for you?

225
00:11:33,776 --> 00:11:35,444
What guy? Excuse me!

226
00:11:35,486 --> 00:11:36,903
We met at a beach club.

227
00:11:36,904 --> 00:11:39,490
It was an organic encounter with a couple of beers

228
00:11:39,532 --> 00:11:41,534
and lots of foam and bubbles!

229
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:42,910
- Okay, fine. - [LEXI] Bubbles!

230
00:11:42,952 --> 00:11:44,328
Whatever you say. Go!

231
00:11:44,537 --> 00:11:45,704
[JAO] You’re going to be late!

232
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:47,039
[LEXI] What’s so funny?

233
00:11:47,081 --> 00:11:49,667
- Text me when you get there, okay? - [LEXI] Okay, bye!

234
00:11:49,708 --> 00:11:51,085
[LEXI] Bye, Kara!

235
00:12:13,315 --> 00:12:14,692
[QUINITO] The waves were awesome earlier, bro!

236
00:12:14,733 --> 00:12:16,526
Yeah! It’s intense!

237
00:12:16,527 --> 00:12:17,528
[QUINITO LAUGHS]

238
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:19,738
By the way, did…

239
00:12:20,114 --> 00:12:22,408
Did Pearl leave early?

240
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:26,036
Yeah, she met Ariel a while ago.

241
00:12:26,454 --> 00:12:27,955
[QUINITO] Hm... So...

242
00:12:28,622 --> 00:12:30,750
Gaia is open today?

243
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:33,878
No, Ariel met some tourist from Manila.

244
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:36,297
They will party at El Lobo later.

245
00:12:36,338 --> 00:12:37,631
Oh...

246
00:12:50,895 --> 00:12:52,188
How are you, brother?

247
00:12:52,563 --> 00:12:54,732
I’m cool, bro. I’m actually happy.

248
00:12:54,774 --> 00:12:55,649
[HAN BIN] Oh…

249
00:12:55,650 --> 00:12:57,484
I thought you’re heartbroken.

250
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:58,486
[QUINITO LAUGHS]

251
00:13:00,154 --> 00:13:01,530
Maybe a little bit.

252
00:13:03,115 --> 00:13:04,617
But, for real, though,

253
00:13:04,867 --> 00:13:06,243
I’m actually feeling good.

254
00:13:06,285 --> 00:13:07,285
[QUINITO] Even though…

255
00:13:07,286 --> 00:13:08,120
[QUINITO CLICKS TONGUE]

256
00:13:08,121 --> 00:13:10,330
[QUINITO SIGHS] Pearl rejected me, I feel like,

257
00:13:10,331 --> 00:13:12,166
you know, there’s a reset button.

258
00:13:12,708 --> 00:13:14,418
I can finally focus on my goal.

259
00:13:14,627 --> 00:13:15,920
I’m happy for you, bro.

260
00:13:15,961 --> 00:13:16,962
[QUINITO] Yeah, I mean...

261
00:13:17,004 --> 00:13:18,547
I’m actually happy, too, that

262
00:13:18,797 --> 00:13:20,382
Pearl and I are not awkward anymore.

263
00:13:20,883 --> 00:13:21,884
[HAN BIN] That’s good.

264
00:13:23,093 --> 00:13:24,303
But, you know,

265
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:27,431
I think I know why she…

266
00:13:27,473 --> 00:13:29,058
[QUINITO CLICKS TONGUE] ...friendzoned me.

267
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:32,019
Really? Why?

268
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:35,648
Because I think she likes someone else.

269
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:39,151
You think so?

270
00:13:40,653 --> 00:13:42,071
I know so, brother.

271
00:14:00,172 --> 00:14:07,387
[HAN BIN WHISTLES]

272
00:14:07,388 --> 00:14:09,890
[HAN BIN GRUNTS]

273
00:14:13,310 --> 00:14:15,604
[HAN BIN HUMS]

274
00:14:35,249 --> 00:14:36,250
[HAN BIN SIGHS]

275
00:14:47,678 --> 00:14:48,804
[HAN BIN EXHALES]

276
00:15:08,198 --> 00:15:10,576
[JAO] Kind of random that you brought me here.

277
00:15:12,119 --> 00:15:13,120
[KARA] Not really.

278
00:15:13,746 --> 00:15:17,166
I just wanted you to see Cabitoonan at sunset.

279
00:15:19,543 --> 00:15:21,045
Beautiful, right?

280
00:15:22,379 --> 00:15:25,090
[JAO] The magic of this place never seems to run out.

281
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:34,099
[KARA] You know, Noah and I got approval for our mangrove project.

282
00:15:34,141 --> 00:15:35,809
[JAO] Wow, congratulations!

283
00:15:35,851 --> 00:15:37,226
[KARA] We just need the permit.

284
00:15:37,936 --> 00:15:40,397
[JAO] That means more mangroves for Siargao!

285
00:15:40,439 --> 00:15:41,440
[KARA] Exactly.

286
00:15:52,743 --> 00:15:53,744
What?

287
00:15:55,287 --> 00:15:56,789
Nothing. It’s just that...

288
00:15:57,498 --> 00:16:00,501
your smile’s prettier than the sunset.

289
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:04,880
I like seeing you like this, Kara.

290
00:16:05,506 --> 00:16:07,007
I like seeing you happy.

291
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:11,470
The love you have for Siargao is really inspiring.

292
00:16:15,224 --> 00:16:17,226
I’m happy that you’re here, Jao.

293
00:16:20,562 --> 00:16:22,356
I’m thankful you came back.

294
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:11,822
[KARA AND JAO CHUCKLE]

295
00:17:36,054 --> 00:17:37,139
[JAO SPEAKS SIARGAONON] Good morning.

296
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:38,474
What’s the occasion?

297
00:17:38,515 --> 00:17:40,893
Nothing. I just wanted to give you flowers.

298
00:17:40,934 --> 00:17:42,727
Should I pick you up after your tour?

299
00:17:42,728 --> 00:17:44,730
Jao, I’m not used to being babied.

300
00:17:44,772 --> 00:17:47,066
Nothing has to change just because...

301
00:17:47,483 --> 00:17:48,775
You’re almost there, Pearl.

302
00:17:48,776 --> 00:17:49,985
You have the right words.

303
00:17:50,068 --> 00:17:52,070
I will finish this some other time.

304
00:17:52,112 --> 00:17:55,114
I just need to get ready for our celebration later.

305
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:56,532
[HAN BIN] Good morning, guys!

306
00:17:56,533 --> 00:17:57,951
[JAO] Happy anniversary!

307
00:17:57,993 --> 00:17:58,993
[KARA] You see this?

308
00:17:58,994 --> 00:18:00,996
They all have jobs because of you.

309
00:18:01,038 --> 00:18:02,538
[SIARGAONON] Thank you very much, Han Bin.

310
00:18:02,539 --> 00:18:04,957
You guys all mean so much to me.

311
00:18:04,958 --> 00:18:05,751
[HAN BIN] Thank you, Kara.

312
00:18:05,793 --> 00:18:09,588
[PEOPLE CHEERING]

313
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:10,630
[JAO] Wait, wait!

314
00:18:10,631 --> 00:18:13,133
- Pearl, it’s beautiful, right? - Yeah.

315
00:18:13,175 --> 00:18:14,675
And your story’s beautiful, too.

316
00:18:14,676 --> 00:18:15,677
Tell me more, okay?

317
00:18:15,719 --> 00:18:17,721
What are you even doing? Let’s go.

318
00:18:18,055 --> 00:18:19,264
[MAN] Caitlyn?
